            <ArticleTitle>Design and synthesis of novel pyrimidine analogs as highly selective, non-covalent BTK inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>145-151</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(17)31136-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2017.11.037</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>BTK is a promising target for the treatment of multiple diseases such as B cell malignances, asthma, and rheumatoid arthritis. Here, we report the discovery of a series of novel pyrimidine analogs as potent, highly selective, non-covalent inhibitors of BTK. Compound 25d demonstrated higher affinity to an unactivated conformation of BTK that resulted in an excellent kinase selectivity. Compound 25d showed a good oral bioavailability in mice, and significantly inhibits the PCA reaction in mice.</AbstractText>
